                <cvss_temporal_vector>CVSS2#E:POC/RL:OF/RC:C</cvss_temporal_vector>
                <cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:M/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P</cvss_vector>
                <description>According to its banner, the version of PHP installed on the remote host is earlier than
                    5.3.11, and as such is potentially affected by multiple vulnerabilities :

                    - During the import of environment variables, temporary changes to the &apos;magic_quotes_gpc&apos;
                    directive are not handled properly. This can lower the difficulty for SQL injection attacks.
                    (CVE-2012-0831)

                    - The &apos;$_FILES&apos; variable can be corrupted because the names of uploaded files are not
                    properly validated.
                    (CVE-2012-1172)

                    - The &apos;open_basedir&apos; directive is not properly handled by the functions &apos;readline_write_history&apos;
                    and &apos;readline_read_history&apos;.

                    - The &apos;header()&apos; function does not detect multi-line headers with a CR. (Bug #60227 /
                    CVE-2011-1398)
                </description>
